applied. [Data: Entities (929, 930, 931); Relationships (1933, 1935, 1936, 2007)]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Ferrite grain refinement depends on deformation temperature and Mn.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Ferrite grain refinement refines ferrite grains and is promoted by Mn. At higher deformation temperatures where T_кп > 1000°C, ferrite grain refinement does not occur and austenite homogenizes. When T_кп decreases to 850°C, ferrite grains refine and strength increases; T_xp also decreases under this condition. [Data: Entities (945, 958, 1457, 1458, 1449); Relationships (2015, 3049, 3053, 3055, 2014)]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Mn and Ni content control microstructure from α-structure to bainite.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Low Mn and/or Ni content produces an α-structure with weak texture intensity. Increasing Mn and/or Ni content makes the microstructure bainitic and develops {332}113) and {311}011〉 orientations. This shows composition-driven microstructural and textural transitions. [Data: Entities (684, 180, 681, 685, 658); Relationships (1338, 1339, 1340, 1306, 1307); Entities (665, 666)]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"summary\": \"Inclusions contribute to anisotropy and embrittlement, with cracking along {100} grains.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Manganese sulphide forms inclusions that are flattened by low-temperature rolling. Inclusions contribute to plane anisotropy and through-thickness embrittlement. Cracks can propagate along grains with {100} orientation. [Data: Entities (1196, 1195, 786, 813); Relationships (2595, 2594, 1552, 1606)]\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 6208, "completion_tokens": 6291, "total_tokens": 12499, "compute_duration_seconds": 30.527432918548584, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}